Subject: [overlay 0022] visionOS VR core — head pose, per-eye tangents, VR gates

The whole engine-side delta for the visionOS VR mode, gated on a single state block
(q2vr, inc/shared/shared.h) that ONLY a visionOS VR world frame ever sets. Every other
configuration — iOS, the macOS oracle, the visionOS 2D window, the visionOS 3D panel —
leaves it zero and takes byte-for-byte the paths it takes today.

  * q2_vr_state_t + the global instance (shared.h, common/math.c). One struct, written by
    the platform shell, read by the client and the renderer. Deliberately NOT cvars:
    cl_kickangles, cl_thirdperson and gl_znear are CVAR_CHEAT and are silently refused on
    a multiplayer server, so a VR override expressed as a cvar write would work in single
    player and vanish online.
  * Matrix_FrustumTangents (common/math.c) — the asymmetric per-eye projection, from the
    compositor's four edge tangents in X *and* Y. GL_Frustum takes it under the VR gate,
    with the near plane read from q2vr.znear and the far plane published back in
    q2vr.zfar_used so the composite's forward-Z -> reverse-infinite conversion uses the
    number this frame rendered with (it changes per map).
  * The stereo-convergence window skew is skipped in VR: the tangents already encode the
    eye offset, and skewing again double-counts it.
  * GL_SetupFrustumTangents (refresh/main.c) — culling planes built from the real per-eye
    tangents instead of half a symmetric FOV. This is the black-wedge-past-85-degrees
    class; the eye frusta are asymmetric and canted, so the fov/2 cone rejects geometry
    the eye can actually see.
  * setup_weaponmodel renders the gun in the WORLD frustum in VR (cl_gunfov re-projection
    is a flat-screen affordance that breaks stereo scale and lies about depth), and the
    RF_DEPTHHACK depth-range squash is disabled — the compositor reprojects against depth,
    and a squashed value makes the weapon swim against the world on every head movement.
  * Head pose written as ordinary refdef viewangles + an origin OFFSET at the site overlay
    0016 already owns (client/view.c). refdef_t carries Euler angles and the renderer
    derives its basis from them, so this is the entire pose seam. The offset form keeps
    prediction, the view-height ramp and the damage view drop working.
  * Audio listener basis substituted for the head basis (client/entities.c) so sound
    sources stay put in the room when the body turns under a still head.

Apply: patch -p1 -d vendor/q2repro < this
